{"ts": 1789777714.0194829, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "This is very reassuring. The sign structure is coherent and economically sensible:\n\n- Every sign flip **degrades** performance monotonically in proportion to the flipped feature's standalone strength (flipping 38, the strongest, is most destructive: 1.106 \u2192 0.102).\n- Pairs among {13, 3, 1} without 38 still produce 0.67\u20130.86 \u2014 these features carry real independent signal, not noise that happens to align.\n- The combination gains are consistent with diversifying imperfectly-correlated positive-Sharpe signals, roughly what \u221a-scaling would predict.\n\nThis is not a case where I found a fragile needle. Let me do one focused check on whether a better third feature exists, then stop \u2014 additional mining would inflate the search-adjusted bar and add overfitting without real gain."}
